148: ## MobileWorld
149: 
150: Secondary and descriptive: 105 English GUI-only tasks, one run per model, temperature 0, 50 rounds per task.
151: This compares agent pipelines, not model weights alone. Source:
152: [`results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md`](../results/mobileworld/mw_r2_comparison.md) (+ `.json`).
153: 
154: ### Scores
155: 
156: | Model | Successes / 105 | Tasks with a result | No result (counted as failure) |
157: |---|---|---|---|
158: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B (official agent) | **22 (21.0%)** | 102 | 3 |
159: | MAI-UI-2B (official agent, 8-bit) | 11 (10.5%) | 98 | 7 |
160: | LFM3-VL-2B v4 | 6 (5.7%) | 104 | 1 |
161: 
162: ### Paired comparisons (exact McNemar)
163: 
164: | Comparison | Both solved | Only first | Only second | Difference | p |
165: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
166: | v4 vs GUI-Owl | 6 | 0 | 16 | −15.2 pts | 3.05 × 10⁻⁵ |
167: | MAI-UI vs v4 | 4 | 7 | 2 | +4.8 pts | 0.18 |
168: | MAI-UI vs GUI-Owl | 9 | 2 | 13 | −10.5 pts | 0.0074 |
169: 
170: ### Sensitivity (environment problems)
171: 
172: | Tasks kept | v4 | GUI-Owl | MAI-UI |
173: |---|---|---|---|
174: | All 105 | 6 | 22 | 11 |
175: | 97: drop tasks with a setup/scoring failure in the v4 or GUI-Owl run | 6 | 22 | — |
176: | 87: also drop tasks where v4's or GUI-Owl's device was re-initialised | 5 | 21 | — |
177: | 89: drop the 16 tasks with an environment problem in MAI-UI's run | 6 | 21 | 11 |
178: 
179: - **What-if, not a bound:** if MAI-UI had solved the 5 tasks it lost to final setup failures, it would score 16
180:   vs GUI-Owl's 22 (p = 0.26). GUI-Owl and v4 solved none of those 5.
181: - MAI-UI ran last, on recreated containers after two spot-VM preemptions. Its emulators crashed with a fatal KVM
182:   error 17 times. The GUI-Owl and v4 container logs no longer exist, so whether they saw the same crashes is unknown.
183: 
184: ### Settings per model
185: 
186: | Setting | v4 | GUI-Owl | MAI-UI |
187: |---|---|---|---|
188: | Screenshots per step | 1 | 1 (official default) | 1 (official default 3) |
189: | Text history | last 8 intent/action pairs | all earlier step summaries | official |
190: | Image budget | ≤ 880×880 px area, ≤ 1,024 tokens | full screen, ≤ 2,600 tokens | full screen, ≤ 2,600 tokens |
191: | Weights | 4-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit |
192: | Parse attempts | 2 | 5 | official |
193: 
194: ### Harness notes (disclosed, not corrected)
195: 
196: - **No user simulator:** `ask_user` needs an LLM-backed simulator this setup lacks. GUI-Owl hit it in 7 executions
197:   and MAI-UI in 14. v4 has no such action.
198: - **Typing and Enter cost v4 rounds:** its adapter sends Enter as an extra round after typing. In 3 tasks the
199:   Enter fell on round 50 and was never sent. 37 tasks that hit the budget had fewer than 50 model decisions.
200: - **One task fails for every model:** ThanksgivingPrepTask setup failed on every attempt.
201: - **Discarded runs:** v4's first run (5/105) used an adapter that changed v4's scroll and Enter behaviour, so it is
202:   not counted. GUI-Owl's first run lost its model server after 4 tasks and was discarded.
203: 
204: ---
205: 
206: ## Speed
207: 
208: These are small pilot measurements of each model's full pipeline (agent code + server), not controlled benchmarks.
209: v4 sends far fewer prompt tokens per step (a smaller image) and showed higher prompt throughput in these runs; the
210: tests do not isolate why.
211: 
212: ### CPU (Intel Xeon 2.8 GHz, 8 threads, idle GCP n2-standard-16)
213: 
214: Same 5 screenshots and goals for every model, through each model's own evaluation agent; all three at 4-bit
215: (including MAI-UI here), llama.cpp `cd959bae9`. Source: [`results/speed/speed_t8.md`](../results/speed/speed_t8.md).
216: 
217: | Model | Calls kept* | s/step (median) | Prompt tokens | Prompt tokens/s | Output tokens | Server memory |
218: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
219: | **v4** | 14 | **6.4** | 803 | 149 | 28 | 2.8 GB |
220: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | 4 | 58.0 | 2,570 | 47 | 47 | 7.5 GB† |
221: | MAI-UI-2B | 4 | 58.2 | 2,575 | 48 | 90 | 7.4 GB† |
222: 
223: \* Calls answered from llama.cpp's RAM prompt cache were excluded, which left few GUI-Owl / MAI-UI calls.
224: 
225: † Inflated by llama.cpp's RAM prompt cache. Model files are 1.30 GB (v4) and 1.55 GB (GUI-Owl, MAI-UI at 4-bit).
226: 
227: ### Apple M5 GPU, measured inside the AndroidWorld seed-30 runs
228: 
229: Source: [`results/androidworld/dev_seed30_summary.md`](../results/androidworld/dev_seed30_summary.md).
230: 
231: | Model | Weights | Steps timed | s/step median (p10–p90) | Prompt tokens | Output tokens |
232: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
233: | **v4** | 4-bit | 1,706 | **2.96** (1.7–4.6) | 1,303 | 22 |
234: | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | 4-bit | 2,228 | 7.00 (4.6–10.4) | 2,106 | 47 |
235: | MAI-UI-2B | 8-bit | 2,053 | 9.35 (6.2–13.9) | 2,086 | 51 |
236: 
237: ### Phone (Qualcomm reference phone, Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6, CPU, 4 threads)
238: 
239: Model runs on the phone (llama.cpp b12110). Rows are matched on the same median sampled fastest-core frequency
240: (~2.65 GHz), not on a controlled clock. Source: [`results/qdc/speed_qdc_v6.md`](../results/qdc/speed_qdc_v6.md).
241: 
242: | Setting | v4 | GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | MAI-UI-2B (8-bit) |
243: |---|---|---|---|
244: | As evaluated (image ceiling: v4 1,024 tokens, others 2,600) | **~39 s** (10 calls) | ~1,100 s (2 calls) | ~1,063 s (2 calls) |
245: | Same 1,024-token ceiling for all | **~39 s** (10 calls) | ~198 s (10 calls) | ~183 s (10 calls) |
246: 
247: - **The v4 "as evaluated" figure is its equal-ceiling run.** v4's evaluation ceiling is already 1,024 tokens. Its
248:   own earlier "as evaluated" run (27.7 s) ran at a higher sampled frequency, so it is not used.
249: - **Equal-ceiling accuracy is unknown.** GUI-Owl's and MAI-UI's accuracy at a 1,024-token ceiling was not measured,
250:   and equal image-token counts were not verified.
251: - **Prompt caching favours GUI-Owl and MAI-UI.** They reused 460–990 cached prompt tokens per call; v4 reused none.
252: - **Run order:** the sampled fastest-core frequency fell under sustained load (4.03 → 2.65 GHz), so the
253:   equal-ceiling runs used both model orders.
254: - **Pixel 9 attempt:** a partial earlier run (Firebase device streaming) timed v4 only, at 74.4 s/step over 11
255:   calls. GUI-Owl and MAI-UI did not complete, and the cause of the slowdown was not isolated
256:   ([`results/devstream/`](../results/devstream/)).
257: 
258: ---
259: 
260: ## Offline evaluations
261: 
262: ### AndroidControl test (official split, 8,444 steps) and general knowledge
263: 
264: Sources: [`results/SUMMARY.md`](../results/SUMMARY.md), [`results/V2_COMPARISON.md`](../results/V2_COMPARISON.md); v4 from
265: [`results/v4_dev/hub/eval/`](../results/v4_dev/hub/eval/) and
266: [`results/general/lfm3vl2b_v4_retention_logprob.json`](../results/general/lfm3vl2b_v4_retention_logprob.json).
267: Step success rate; history is teacher-forced, so this is an upper bound on closed-loop behaviour.
268: 
269: | Model | High-level step SR | Low-level step SR | "complete" accuracy | MMStar | MMLU |
270: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
271: | LFM3-VL-2B base | 0.313 | 0.634 | 0.000 | 52.1% | 48.9% |
272: | LFM3-VL-2B v1 | 0.715 | 0.948 | 0.792 | 57.1% | 49.5% |
273: | LFM3-VL-2B v2 | 0.716 | 0.893 | 0.732 | 54.6% | 50.9% |
274: | LFM3-VL-2B v3 | 0.723 | 0.902 | 0.725 | 55.3% | 50.0% |
275: | LFM3-VL-2B v4 | 0.728 | 0.908 | 0.716 | 52.9% | 50.4% |
276: | Qwen3.5-2B v1 | 0.734 | 0.949 | 0.784 | 57.3% | 53.7% |
277: | Qwen3.5-0.8B v1 | 0.694 | 0.942 | 0.745 | 48.9% | 45.2% |
278: | LFM2.5-VL-450M v1 | 0.536 | 0.862 | 0.561 | 39.3% | 39.2% |
279: 
280: - **No significant drop in general knowledge** was detected for any fine-tune that was measured (v4-RL was not).
281: - **MMStar:** it rose significantly after fine-tuning for v1, v2, v3 and both Qwen3.5-2B versions. v4's changes
282:   (+0.7 / +1.5 points) are not significant (McNemar p = 0.52 / 0.23). Paired tests and 95% CIs are in `results/general/`.
283: - **v4 vs v1:** v4 is lower on terminal "complete" accuracy (0.716 vs 0.792); the cause was not isolated.
284: 
285: ### v4 development gate and v4-RL promotion
286: 
287: Sources: [`results/v4_gate_seed30.txt`](../results/v4_gate_seed30.txt),
288: [`results/v4rl_promotion_offline.json`](../results/v4rl_promotion_offline.json).
289: 
290: | Check | Threshold | v4 | v4-RL | Result |
291: |---|---|---|---|---|
292: | Strict answer match on 136 held-out questions | v4 ≥ 0.20; RL ≥ v4 + 0.05 | 0.868 | 0.890 | v4 pass; RL fail |
293: | `answer` emitted on those questions | ≥ 0.50 | 0.956 | 1.000 | pass |
294: | False answers on 80 action-goal controls | ≤ 0.03 | 0.00 | 0.00 | pass |
295: | AndroidControl high-level step SR | RL ≥ v4 − 0.02 | 0.728 | 0.667 | RL fail |
296: | AndroidWorld seed 30 | ≥ 3 answer successes; action ≥ v3 − 3 | 6; 12 (v3 13) | — | v4 pass |
297: | AndroidWorld seed 30 total (RL only) | ≥ v4's 18 | — | not run | not reached: RL failed offline |
298: 
299: **Outcome:** v4 was frozen as the final model. v4-RL was not promoted.

