   257	## Secrets and history rewrites
   258	
   259	| Date | What leaked into a run log | Fix |
   260	|---|---|---|
   261	| 2026-11-19 | Environment variables printed by AndroidWorld's setup (an API key, a session token) | Redacted in every commit (`git filter-branch`) |
   262	| 2026-11-20 | An expired Colab file-proxy token inside a download URL | Redacted in every commit (`git filter-branch`) |
   263	
   264	- **Hash maps:** old → new commit hashes are in [history-rewrites.md](history-rewrites.md).
   265	- **Scan:** two independent scans (ours and Codex's) found no credentials. They covered every file in every commit
   266	  reachable from `main` and the archive tag, including compressed episode files.
   267	  - Checked: cloud keys, Hugging Face / OpenAI / Anthropic / GitHub / Google / Modal tokens, private keys, JWTs and
   268	    key/token/secret/password assignments.
   269	  - Not checked: images (no OCR).
   270	- **Owner identity:** the owner's git e-mail appears in commit author fields and in Codex logs that captured `git log`.
   271	- **Automatic redaction on commit (limited).** `.gitattributes` runs the `redact-env` clean filter on `*.log` files
   272	  only, and only where it is configured locally:
   273	  - It redacts `'NAME_WITH_KEY|TOKEN|SECRET|PASSWORD': '…'` pairs (the format AndroidWorld prints) and JWT-shaped
   274	    tokens.
   275	  - It does **not** catch other formats (e.g. `HF_TOKEN=…`, lowercase JSON keys).
   276	  - Run a scan before publishing. One-time setup:
   277	
   278	```bash
   279	git config filter.redact-env.clean "LC_ALL=C sed -E -e \"s/'([A-Z0-9_]*(KEY|TOKEN|SECRET|PASSWORD)[A-Z0-9_]*)': '[^']*'/'\\\\1': '<redacted>'/g\" -e 's/eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{15,}[.]eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{15,}[.][A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}/<redacted-token>/g'"
   280	git config filter.redact-env.smudge cat
   281	```
   282	
